  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O that thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wert",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as my brother, that was nourished at the breasts of my mother! ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I should find thee without, I would kiss thee; yes, I should not be despised.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would lead thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bring thee into my mother's house, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would instruct me: I would cause thee to drink of spiced wine of the juice of my pomegranate.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His left hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "should be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under my head, and his right hand should embrace me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, that ye stir not, nor awake ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love, until he please.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this that cometh up from the wilderness, leaning upon her beloved? I raised thee up under the apple-tree: there thy mother brought thee forth: there she brought thee forth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bore thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Set me as a seal upon thy heart, as a seal upon thy arm: for love ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strong as death; jealousy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cruel as the grave: the coals of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " coals of fire, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a most vehement flame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if a man would give all the substance of his house for love, it would utterly be contemned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have a little sister, and she hath no breasts: what shall we do for our sister in the day when she shall be spoken for?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wall, we will build upon her a palace of silver: and if she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a door, we will inclose her with boards of cedar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wall, and my breasts like towers: then was I in his eyes as one that found favor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Solomon had a vineyard at Baal-hamon; he let out the vineyard to keepers; every one for the fruit of it was to bring a thousand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pieces",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My vineyard which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before me: thou, O Solomon, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "must have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a thousand, and those that keep the fruit of it two hundred.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou that dwellest in the gardens, the companions hearken to thy voice: cause me to hear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make haste, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart upon the mountains of spices.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
